      "updated": 1792842245154,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🛒 ShopHub AI - LangGraph Multi-Agent Order Support",
      "fontSize": 46,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🛒 ShopHub AI - LangGraph Multi-Agent Order Support",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a0"
    },
    {
      "id": "tex2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 42.85714285714289,
      "y": 118.57142857142856,
      "width": 1200.275390625,
      "height": 852.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1202102036,
      "version": 766,
      "versionNonce": 1372564739,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792910343720,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is a multi-agent order support assistant for multi-merchant e-commerce. It turns a support\nagent's natural-language question into a safe, merchant-scoped answer, and routes refund / cancel\nrequests through human approval. The project uses a multi-agent workflow built with LangGraph.\n\n## Problem statement?\n\nImagine ShopHub is a platform used by independent online stores.\n\n - Merchant A - UrbanStyle: sells clothing and accessories.\n - Merchant B - TechNest: sell electronics and computer accessories.\n\nEach merchant has ite own customers, Orders, Staff, and access token. Both use ShopHub's support assistant,\nbut neither merchant can access the other's orders.\n\nExample support conversation:\n\nA support agent at UrbanStyle asks: \"Finds order ORD-2003 and tell me it delivery status.\"\n\nThat order belongs to TechNest, not UrbanStyle.\n\n\nSupporting several merchants usually means jumping between admin panels, order databases and policy\ndocs - and one slip can leak another merchant's data. This project brings that flow into one\nexperience by combining:\n\n- an orders-lookup agent,\n- a refund / cancel proposal agent,\n- a human-approval step (support lead), and\n- a final response agent,\n\nall coordinated through a LangGraph workflow, with the Store API enforcing tenant isolation.",
      "fontSize": 22,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is a multi-agent order support assistant for multi-merchant e-commerce. It turns a support\nagent's natural-language question into a safe, merchant-scoped answer, and routes refund / cancel\nrequests through human approval. The project uses a multi-agent workflow built with LangGraph.\n\n## Problem statement?\n\nImagine ShopHub is a platform used by independent online stores.\n\n - Merchant A - UrbanStyle: sells clothing and accessories.\n - Merchant B - TechNest: sell electronics and computer accessories.\n\nEach merchant has ite own customers, Orders, Staff, and access token. Both use ShopHub's support assistant,\nbut neither merchant can access the other's orders.\n\nExample support conversation:\n\nA support agent at UrbanStyle asks: \"Finds order ORD-2003 and tell me it delivery status.\"\n\nThat order belongs to TechNest, not UrbanStyle.\n\n\nSupporting several merchants usually means jumping between admin panels, order databases and policy\ndocs - and one slip can leak another merchant's data. This project brings that flow into one\nexperience by combining:\n\n- an orders-lookup agent,\n- a refund / cancel proposal agent,\n- a human-approval step (support lead), and\n- a final response agent,\n\nall coordinated through a LangGraph workflow, with the Store API enforcing tenant isolation.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "a1"
    },
    {
